      "body": "Facility to aid clinical trials as Bundibugyo outbreak surpasses 10,000 cases, with nearly 5,000 deaths | Anadolu\nEDITION Belgium deploys mobile lab to Congo to support Ebola vaccine research Africa Europe Belgium deploys mobile lab to Congo to support Ebola vaccine research Facility to aid clinical trials as Bundibugyo outbreak surpasses 10,000 cases, with nearly 5,000 deaths James Tasamba 30 October 2026 • Update : 30 October 2026 RUANDA Belgium is deploying a mobile laboratory to northeastern Democratic Republic of Congo to support research into vaccines and treatments for the Bundibugyo Ebola virus, as the country battles its largest outbreak of the disease, officials said Friday.\nThe facility, destined for Bunia, the capital of Ituri province, will enable researchers to conduct biological analyses on site as part of efforts to develop a safe and effective vaccine, according to Congo's Health Ministry.",
